cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the
  methods paper it accompanies.
type: software
title: "groupunit: correlation, PLS, CCA and similarity analyses with group-level annotations"
abstract: >-
  Python package for designs in which measurements of individuals are related
  to variables that exist only for the groups they belong to. It computes the
  between-group share, the annotation rank and ratio, PLS, CCA and LDA through
  the group means, group shares and effective numbers of groups, the lens null,
  the typicality-pattern decomposition, group-level permutation tests with
  refitting and the pairing ratio, and leave-one-group-out validation.
authors:
  - family-names: Kmecl
    given-names: Tim
    affiliation: Faculty of Mathematics and Physics, University of Ljubljana
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-04"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/timkmecl/groupunit"
url: "https://timkmecl.github.io/groupunit/"
keywords:
  - group-level variables
  - pseudoreplication
  - permutation test
  - partial least squares
  - canonical correlation analysis
  - representational similarity
references:
